MID_EV14_060_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_060_m01_001: There's news, Leilidahna.
MID_EV14_060_m01_002: The White-Maned Demon won his match. He has\nadvanced to the finals.
MID_EV14_060_m01_003: You'll be facing him in the colosseum...just as\nyou desired.
MID_EV14_060_m01_004: Finally. Bertrand will be mine.
MID_EV14_060_m01_005: I will not stop you, as I want you to go on\nwithout regret.
MID_EV14_060_m01_006: Do not die. I could not bear to lose you.
MID_EV14_060_m01_007: I won't die, Kalla. I promise I will return.
MID_EV14_060_m01_008: Oh...
MID_EV14_060_m01_009: That was the Mahdel List you burned, I take it.\nAre you certain you don't need it anymore?
MID_EV14_060_m01_010: I'm sure. I feel like such a fool for being taken in by\nthat damn list.
MID_EV14_060_m01_011: But that doesn't matter now. All that matters is\nkilling Bertrand and making my revenge complete.
MID_EV14_060_m01_012: Is that really all you desire? What about revealing\nthe truth behind the massacre?
MID_EV14_060_m01_013: Of course, but...that's too big a mystery to unravel on\nmy own.
MID_EV14_060_m01_014: If the temples are going to investigate, I'll wait to\nlearn what they discover.
MID_EV14_060_m01_015: I'm sure they are, but... You're not exactly one for the\n"wait and see" approach.
MID_EV14_060_m01_016: There's not much I can do going up against a\nconspiracy, let alone an entire kingdom.
MID_EV14_060_m01_017: True. I hope our recent meeting with Father Mahdel\nat least brought you some closure.
MID_EV14_060_m01_018: There is one thing that struck me as...surprising\nduring your conversation with Kalla.
MID_EV14_060_m01_019: She asked you to survive—but you intend to die in\nthe fight against Bertrand, don't you?
MID_EV14_060_m01_020: You've got the wrong idea about me. I'm not that\nsingle-minded.
MID_EV14_060_m01_021: Leilidahna... Father Mahdel's last words.
MID_EV14_060_m01_022: He said, "Please forgive me."
MID_EV14_060_m01_023: What a lovely thing forgiveness is—such a\nthoroughly human act.
MID_EV14_060_m01_024: Do you believe you can eventually forgive\nFather Mahdel?
MID_EV14_060_m01_025: Hm...
MID_EV14_060_m01_026: It is not easy to forgive someone you loathe, but I\nthink it's the noblest thing a person can do.
MID_EV14_060_m01_027: If everyone could do it, this would be a much\nbetter world. Wouldn't you say?
MID_EV14_060_m01_028: You're asking the wrong person.
MID_EV14_060_m01_029: Let me ask again, Leilidahna. When this is over,\nwhat will you do?
MID_EV14_060_m01_030: I could see you departing on a long journey,\nor working to restore House Cohendia.
MID_EV14_060_m01_031: I can't conceive of that yet. I've been living for my\nrevenge for so long.
MID_EV14_060_m01_032: In that case, you'll have to promise me that you\ncome and challenge me.
MID_EV14_060_m01_033: And we settle once and for all which of us is the\nsuperior Rose of Caelus.
MID_EV14_060_m01_034: Fine. I guess that's not too much to ask.
MID_EV14_061_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_061_m01_001: Hear anything, Tahonia, or is the way clear?
MID_EV14_061_m01_002: I think you can get out if you go right now.
MID_EV14_061_m01_003: You have to be careful—they've been keeping a\ncloser eye on you.
MID_EV14_061_m01_004: Yes. Which is to be expected, after I gave Bertrand\nthe Bloodaxe from the castle.
MID_EV14_061_m01_005: It's unfortunate that the chancellor and Gilchris\nfound out.
MID_EV14_061_m01_006: Really, it was unavoidable that matters would\nescalate in this way.
MID_EV14_061_m01_007: But the increase in patrols certainly won't help.\nIt will be difficult to escape.
MID_EV14_061_m01_008: Where are you going today, can I ask?
MID_EV14_061_m01_009: Well. I keep thinking about what happened with\nLeda the other day.
MID_EV14_061_m01_010: I thought I'd go into town and try to find her.
MID_EV14_061_m01_011: I need to know why she's so intent on\nkilling Bertrand.
MID_EV14_061_m01_012: I'm going to talk to her and learn the whole story.
MID_EV14_061_m01_013: What is it about this woman that has you so hung\nup on her?
MID_EV14_061_m01_014: I...wanted Leda to be my friend.
MID_EV14_061_m01_015: Tahonia, I hate to do this to you, but would you take\nmy place again today?
MID_EV14_061_m01_016: Of course. Anything for you, Queen Aswan.
MID_EV14_061_m01_017: Alright, that should do the trick.
MID_EV14_061_m01_018: Yes, no one will recognize me in this.
MID_EV14_061_m01_019: I'm off now. I leave the rest to you.
MID_EV14_061_m01_020: You got it. Don't worry about things back here—\nI'll take care of everything.
MID_EV14_061_m01_021: Aswan, a moment? I want to discuss our audience\nwith the Divine Sovereign.
MID_EV14_061_m01_022: Y-yes? What is it, Gilchris?
MID_EV14_061_m01_023: What the hell? What's going on here?!
MID_EV14_061_m01_024: Aswan's not that tall. You must be...Tahonia!
MID_EV14_061_m01_025: Tsk. You figured it out. Nothing gets past you,\nYour Majesty.
MID_EV14_061_m01_026: Shut up! Remove that horrible disguise!
MID_EV14_061_m01_027: That must mean Aswan has— No! Has she\ngotten outside?
MID_EV14_061_m01_028: Everyone, the queen has escaped! Dispatch the\nsoldiers to find her. At once!
MID_EV14_062_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_062_m01_001: Leda! Please, wait. I need to speak with you!
MID_EV14_062_m01_002: Aswan? We're done talking.
MID_EV14_062_m01_003: I know you're facing Bertrand in the final match of\nthe Heroic Games.
MID_EV14_062_m01_004: And I can't let it happen without gaining some kind\nof understanding!
MID_EV14_062_m01_005: Why... Why are you so intent on killing him?
MID_EV14_062_m01_006: And what in the world happened to you on the day\nof the banquet?
MID_EV14_062_m01_007: You know very well. It was you who sprung the\ntrap on us.
MID_EV14_062_m01_008: As for who I am...I'm from Kassite. I was there on\nthe day of the Cydonia Massacre.
MID_EV14_062_m01_009: It was a peaceful life, until Arago took that from us.
MID_EV14_062_m01_010: And a happy life—until that man, Bertrand,\nmurdered my father.
MID_EV14_062_m01_011: I swore that nothing would stop me from killing him.
MID_EV14_062_m01_012: But that was— He had no choice, surely. He was\nunder orders from the king!
MID_EV14_062_m01_013: You really think that would be of any comfort to\nhis victims?!
MID_EV14_062_m01_014: Bertrand never even intended to join in the siege!
MID_EV14_062_m01_015: I still remember how terribly fatigued he looked\nwhen he returned.
MID_EV14_062_m01_016: The look of pain and desperation in his eyes.\nThere was no triumph there—he was devastated!
MID_EV14_062_m01_017: Gutted, I'm sure. You're wasting your time!
MID_EV14_062_m01_018: Taking his life is all that keeps me going! And I\nwon't let anyone stop me!
MID_EV14_062_m01_019: Then...I'm sorry, but I will be praying that you fail.\nPraying for Bertrand's victory!
MID_EV14_062_m01_020: Then you're a brazen fool. You know nothing of\nhow I feel!
MID_EV14_062_m01_021: Now stop talking, Aswan, or I'll personally ensure\nthat you do.
MID_EV14_062_m01_022: Mm—
MID_EV14_062_m01_023: You really think that—after all I've done—I'd let\nyou intimidate me?
MID_EV14_062_m01_024: Don't be so stubborn, now. I really will do it.
MID_EV14_062_m01_025: By all means.
MID_EV14_062_m01_026: I'll simply shoot your arrow out of the air.
MID_EV14_062_m01_027: Then there will come another. I'm not joking.
MID_EV14_062_m01_028: As many arrows as you fire, I will shoot down,\nuntil you give up on this quest for revenge.
MID_EV14_062_m01_029: Haaah... Haaah...
MID_EV14_062_m01_030: You're not the prissy princess I thought you were.
MID_EV14_062_m01_031: No, I'm not. And you—I've never seen your intense\nanger from this side before.
MID_EV14_062_m01_032: But it's incorrect to say I have no understanding of\nhow you feel.
MID_EV14_062_m01_033: After all...my father, too, was murdered. In that we\nare the same.
MID_EV14_062_m01_034: Hm?!
MID_EV14_062_m01_035: I would like to know the truth of what happened on\nthat day.
MID_EV14_062_m01_036: But I can't do it alone—the pull of fate is too strong.
MID_EV14_062_m01_037: I need Bertrand's help.
MID_EV14_062_m01_038: So as pained as I am to oppose you, I must believe\nthat Bertrand will win.
MID_EV14_062_m01_039: Queen Aswan! She's over here!
MID_EV14_062_m01_040: The king was so concerned for your well-being.\nWhy don't you come with us?
MID_EV14_062_m01_041: Leda, I beg you, forgive him!
MID_EV14_062_m01_042: This way, this way. Everyone's waiting.
MID_EV14_062_m01_043: Forgive him?
MID_EV14_062_m01_044: What a pathetic joke. No— There's no way I would\nlet him return to you.
MID_EV14_063_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_063_m01_001: The match is starting.
MID_EV14_063_m01_002: Bertrand, Leda... Please stay alive. Both of you.
MID_EV14_063_m01_003: Who is this woman Bertrand's fighting? She better\nbe damn good!
MID_EV14_063_m01_004: If Bertrand wins, he'll be acquitted and released—it\nwould be a disaster!
MID_EV14_063_m01_005: We've got to stop this! Where the hell is Stepmother?
MID_EV14_063_m01_006: Haha! Here we are. Finally, just you and me. Oh, you\nhave no idea how long I've been waiting for this.
MID_EV14_063_m01_007: Look at you though. You've changed—that white\nhair, those eyes, your entire demeanor.
MID_EV14_063_m01_008: So much time has passed between then and now.\nI bet you've been through a lot.
MID_EV14_063_m01_009: I know I have. But now, here you are...within\nmy reach...
MID_EV14_063_m01_010: Who are you? I don't believe I recognize you.
MID_EV14_063_m01_011: Who am I? What a cruel thing to say. I remember\nyou so clearly. I mean, how could I not?
MID_EV14_063_m01_012: I suppose that's just how thieves are. They never\nthink about the losses they inflict.
MID_EV14_063_m01_013: Put your hand on your heart and think...think about\nwhat you did that day in Cydonia.
MID_EV14_063_m01_014: Cydonia? You mean, you...
MID_EV14_063_m01_015: Your face and your voice— I will never forget you!\nI'll kill you. I will!
MID_EV14_063_m01_016: Indigo hair, eyes like emeralds... You're Guillermo's\ndaughter.
MID_EV14_063_m01_017: Ever since that day, I've been looking for you.\nAnd finally...I've found you.
MID_EV14_063_m01_018: You know, I was told that you'd been executed. \nIn that moment, everything turned pitch black.
MID_EV14_063_m01_019: It was like all the color drained from the world. And\nthat colorless place is where I lived for a long time.
MID_EV14_063_m01_020: Then one day, Kalla told me you were still alive,\nand the color came flooding back...
MID_EV14_063_m01_021: The color of the flames and the blood. That vivid,\nmerciless red. The red of my hatred.
MID_EV14_063_m01_022: I'm glad I started down this path. Yes, I've been\nthrough a lot, but it's brought me here...to you.
MID_EV14_063_m01_023: Now I can plunge my blade into your chest and\ndrain every last drop of your blood.
MID_EV14_063_m01_024: The girl from that day, standing before me here?\nI never imagined this would happen.
MID_EV14_063_m01_025: But there's someone I have to get back to. I won't just\nlie down and die.
MID_EV14_063_m01_026: The betrayal of my father...the suffering of the\nCydonians...this relentless hatred I can't let go of...
MID_EV14_063_m01_027: I will carve them into your heart like a beautiful,\nterrible letter—and then send you to hell!
MID_EV14_064_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_064_m01_001: End him! What are you doing? What in the hell are\nyou waiting for?!
MID_EV14_064_m01_002: Bring the dagger down. That's all you have to do.\nStop hesitating!
MID_EV14_064_m01_003: Oh, Leda. I wasn't sure.
MID_EV14_064_m01_004: Why haven't you killed me?
MID_EV14_064_m01_005: I need you to tell me what happened that day.\nWhat were you doing in Cydonia?
MID_EV14_064_m01_006: Why did you fight my father, and what did he say?
MID_EV14_064_m01_007: My friend Gilchris asked me to join the siege in\nhis stead. That's why I was there.
MID_EV14_064_m01_008: After arriving, I tried talking to Viceroy Guillermo,\nand the two of us started making progress.
MID_EV14_064_m01_009: But then...the worst happened. An arrow flew at us\nfrom a Cydonian tower, sparking a battle.
MID_EV14_064_m01_010: I know all this. Keep going.
MID_EV14_064_m01_011: As the generals of opposing armies, we had to face\neach other in battle.
MID_EV14_064_m01_012: I...defeated him. With his last breath, all he asked\nwas that I protect his daughter.
MID_EV14_064_m01_013: Oh... Father.
MID_EV14_064_m01_014: After you escaped, the Aragonian army started\nraiding the surrounding areas.
MID_EV14_064_m01_015: I ordered my soldiers to look for you, and shouted\nat my superiors to stop the pillaging.
MID_EV14_064_m01_016: But I couldn't stop it. And I couldn't find you.
MID_EV14_064_m01_017: I returned to the royal capital feeling crushed by my\nown powerlessness.
MID_EV14_064_m01_018: And awaiting me there—a murdered king. I was\nsoon arrested for regicide.
MID_EV14_064_m01_019: I didn't understand why this was happening to me.\nIt was a conspiracy, I later learned.
MID_EV14_064_m01_020: In a craven bid for power, Gilchris—the man I\nconsidered my closest friend—had framed me.
MID_EV14_064_m01_021: I think I see the shape of it now.
MID_EV14_064_m01_022: You got set up. Don't you think you might be a little\ntoo trusting?
MID_EV14_064_m01_023: You're not the first to say so.
MID_EV14_064_m01_024: At the center of all this, there's one fact that you\ncan't explain away.
MID_EV14_064_m01_025: You were the one who killed my father.
MID_EV14_064_m01_026: Yes... Yes, I was.
MID_EV14_064_m01_027: Rghhh...
MID_EV14_064_m01_028: But I suppose it's possible that your enemy and mine\nare one and the same.
MID_EV14_064_m01_029: What do you mean?
MID_EV14_064_m01_030: You have time now. Aswan wants me to leave\nyou alive, so I will.
MID_EV14_064_m01_031: Struggle, Bertrand. Fight your true enemies.
MID_EV14_064_m01_032: But you will die by my hand one day. Never\nforget that.
MID_EV14_064_m01_033: In time, I'll lay the White-Maned Demon's head upon\nmy father's grave.
MID_EV14_064_m01_034: Are you sure this is what you want?
MID_EV14_064_m01_035: Stop talking before I change my mind.
MID_EV14_064_m01_036: Damn it! Bertrand, the bastard. Still getting off\nunscathed—after THAT?!
MID_EV14_064_m01_037: {SetColor=Gray}Thank you, Leda. Oh, thank you...{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV14_064_m01_038: Your beloved lives for now, Aswan.
MID_EV14_064_m01_039: That doesn't mean I forgive him.
MID_EV14_064_m01_040: From the games' many pitched battles, a clear\nvictor emerges.
MID_EV14_064_m01_041: Standing strong in her triumph—Leda of\nRose Tempest!
MID_EV14_065_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_065_m01_001: Leda, allow me to congratulate you on your victory,\nand the magnificent fight that preceded it.
MID_EV14_065_m01_002: I've no doubt that will go down as one of the greatest\nmatches in the arena's history.
MID_EV14_065_m01_028: To mark this, as Divine Sovereign, I bestow upon\nyou the moniker Flame Lord of Dagda.
MID_EV14_065_m01_029: For your amazing skill with the vihuela, you will be\nknown by all as the Siren of the Six-String.
MID_EV14_065_m01_003: Thank you, Divine Sovereign. Now...as for my wish.
MID_EV14_065_m01_004: Last we spoke, you said your deepest wish was to\nface Bertrand.
MID_EV14_065_m01_005: That has come to pass—albeit by chance. Leaving\nthe matter of your father's honor, I believe?
MID_EV14_065_m01_006: Yes. My companion, the vulkan Syracusio, will\nsubmit the evidence we have obtained.
MID_EV14_065_m01_007: I would request that you reopen your investigation\ninto the events that led to the Cydonia Massacre.
MID_EV14_065_m01_008: You'll find that my father was framed.
MID_EV14_065_m01_009: When you do, I'd like you to restore Viceroy\nGuillermo's good name.
MID_EV14_065_m01_010: Very well. I will grant this request.
MID_EV14_065_m01_011: I promise the temples will thoroughly investigate\nthe matter, and punish those responsible.
MID_EV14_065_m01_012: In fact...since we last spoke, I've been looking into\nthe situation on my own.
MID_EV14_065_m01_013: From what's come to light, it's clear enough the\nempire cannot ignore this matter.
MID_EV14_065_m01_014: The conspiracy was larger than I imagined. I know\nnot how deeply we'll need to investigate the temples.
MID_EV14_065_m01_015: The investigation will not be easy, nor without\nits dangers.
MID_EV14_065_m01_016: But we must cut out whatever evil has found\npurchase in the Dagdan Empire.
MID_EV14_065_m01_017: So, yes. I will do as you ask, and bring the truth of\nthe tragedy in Cydonia to light.
MID_EV14_065_m01_018: Thank you. What you're doing will bring peace to\nmy father's soul, and the other victims'.
MID_EV14_065_m01_019: Leda, one last matter. Your house, Cohendia, has a\nstoried lineage and ties to Kalla.
MID_EV14_065_m01_020: Would you like me to restore its place among the\nnoble houses?
MID_EV14_065_m01_021: I appreciate the offer, but...I can't give you\nan answer at the moment.
MID_EV14_065_m01_022: I'm not ready to take up my father's mantle as the\nhead of the house.
MID_EV14_065_m01_023: Not before I've seen more of the world.
MID_EV14_065_m01_024: I think for now, I'll travel across Dagda seeking my\nown song, like my ancestor Cohen did.
MID_EV14_065_m01_025: That's a fine idea. There's no better way to learn\nthan going on a journey.
MID_EV14_065_m01_026: And after you've gotten some answers, and returned\nback here...
MID_EV14_065_m01_027: I shall endeavor to have some good news for you.
MID_EV14_066_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_066_m01_001: That ought to do it.
MID_EV14_066_m01_002: Well done, milady. I'd only suggest adding a few\nstones so the animals can't dig it up.
MID_EV14_066_m01_003: Nice spot. All the flowers.
MID_EV14_066_m01_004: Linaria, to be precise! And so many. I wonder who\nplanted them here?
MID_EV14_066_m01_005: Lord Guillermo visited this hill often when he was\na praetor.
MID_EV14_066_m01_006: He and your mother, Hilaria, used to sit here and\nwatch the sun set.
MID_EV14_066_m01_007: <NCA>Think.
MID_EV14_066_m01_008: My father's soul is still imprisoned by Balor in the\nunderworld.
MID_EV14_066_m01_009: It feels like meager consolation, doing this.
MID_EV14_066_m01_010: It is all you can do. No doubt your father would be\npleased that he's been buried properly.
MID_EV14_066_m01_011: But...I have something to report, Miss Leda.
MID_EV14_066_m01_012: The Order of Mithras's headquarters. Word is it\nburned down, causing a stir at the port.
MID_EV14_066_m01_016: And a woman's body was found amidst\nthe wreckage.
MID_EV14_066_m01_017: Maria's, it's said.
MID_EV14_066_m01_018: That's not possible! You're saying...she's dead?!
MID_EV14_066_m01_019: Meanwhile, the kingdom of Arago is scrambling in\nthe absence of its chancellor.
MID_EV14_066_m01_020: Her faction, which was in control to this point,\nis rapidly losing power, and tensions are rising.
MID_EV14_066_m01_022: Maria and Martila going missing at the same time.\nI suppose that confirms it.
MID_EV14_066_m01_023: I do find it hard to believe she could be killed\nso easily, but the evidence paints a clear picture.
MID_EV14_066_m01_024: So, the only mastermind behind Cydonia that we\nknow of is dead already.
MID_EV14_066_m01_025: Heh...
MID_EV14_066_m01_026: What now, milady? I will attend you until I die.
MID_EV14_066_m01_027: I don't have a destination in mind. South, I suppose?
MID_EV14_066_m01_028: I hear there are many people there faithful to\nYu Phas, the Keeper of Death and Night.
MID_EV14_066_m01_029: Maybe we could find some clue to freeing my father's\nsoul from the underworld.
MID_EV14_066_m01_030: I'm sorry, but how long are you all planning to\nfollow me around?
MID_EV14_066_m01_031: My lady requested that I accompany you. So,\nI ought to keep at it, don't you think?
MID_EV14_066_m01_032: Oh, are you "accompanying" me? I think it's more\nlike following me around.
MID_EV14_066_m01_035: Hah hah! Leilidahna! Surely you've not forgotten\nyour promise.
MID_EV14_066_m01_036: I have no intention of leaving your side until you are\nutterly bested!
MID_EV14_066_m01_037: Besides! Your soul is corrupted by that treasure of\nDrake's in your possession.
MID_EV14_066_m01_038: You'll need someone to prevent you from going on\na rampage!
MID_EV14_066_m01_039: And that's supposed to be you, huh? Alright.
MID_EV14_066_m01_052: In any case, it may be best to keep Obsidian sealed\nfor the time being.
MID_EV14_066_m01_053: You may be able to slow the progression of your\nsymptoms if you refrain from unnecessary use.
MID_EV14_066_m01_040: What about you, Mu? Shouldn't you go back to\nyour mother?
MID_EV14_066_m01_041: I... I thought about it. But I think I'd prefer sticking\nwith you.
MID_EV14_066_m01_042: I've learned more from this journey than I would in\nany book.
MID_EV14_066_m01_043: Well, you're bound to learn a lot about bugs. I hear\nthey're plentiful in the southern forests.
MID_EV14_066_m01_044: B-bugs? Oh stars. How deplorable!
MID_EV14_066_m01_045: That's fine! Bugs are weird, so I kinda like 'em!
MID_EV14_066_m01_046: Speaking of which—I have to ask.
MID_EV14_066_m01_047: Leda, do you like Bertrand?
MID_EV14_066_m01_048: What? Don't be ridiculous. I despise that man!
MID_EV14_066_m01_049: Ah, OK. Just...seemed like you had a lot in common.
MID_EV14_066_m01_050: That's because you're a kid, and you don't understand\ngrown-up matters. Come on.
MID_EV14_066_m01_051: Hey! Leda, hold up!
MID_NR14_02_m01: <SH>
MID_NR14_02_m01_001: I can't count the number of times in my life I\nwanted to die.
MID_NR14_02_m01_002: When I stared into the abyss, it was only my hatred\nthat kept me going.
MID_NR14_02_m01_003: Now, the more I use Obsidian, the more my soul is\neaten away by the curse I inherited.
MID_NR14_02_m01_004: I wonder. How much longer can I survive?
MID_NR14_02_m01_005: How much further can I go?
MID_NR14_02_m01_006: I don't know. But I do know this.
MID_NR14_02_m01_007: I will live. As long as, somewhere in this world,\nyou're alive too.